//@ run-pass
//@ timeout: 180
//@ expect-stdout-contains: CIRC28_DRUG_VANCOMYCIN_PASS
//
// CURRENT STATE: ROUND 3 (block further down); the round 1 and round 2 text is kept as the record.
// Vancomycin on the circ28 drug record (stdlib/darwin_pbpk/circ28_drug_vancomycin.sio). Renal
// route (observed renal clearance 89 mL/min acting on arterial plasma) plus a declared,
// unidentified non-renal plasma clearance; distribution on an INTERSTITIAL pattern x one scalar.
// Units mg, L, h. Parameter table, sources and status: module header.
//
// FITTED (so NOT validations; each to ONE observable):
//   V_ss 59.13 L (Matzke 1984, midpoint of 0.72-0.90 L/kg x 73 kg)   -> kpsc, closed form
//   central volume V1 10.95 L (Matzke 1986 review, 0.15 L/kg x 73)   -> pssc, by curve peeling
//                                                            of a bolus (windows fixed a priori)
// MEASURED/DERIVED, not fitted: cl_renal 5.34 L/h (Golper 1988), non-renal plasma clearance
//   0.6774 L/h (mean of Rodvold 1988 and the label; Golper's 42 mL/min is not corroborated),
//   bp 0.55 (UNSOURCED: 1 - Hct).
//
// DISCLOSURE OF WHAT WAS SEEN BEFORE THESE EXPECTATIONS WERE WRITTEN. A scan of pssc was run to
// choose the fit: kpsc = 5.447; pssc 0.0005 / 0.002 / 0.01 / 0.05 / 0.2 / 1.0 gave peeled V1 10.5 /
// 13.9 / 33.1 / 50.6 / 53.6 / 54.2 L, terminal half-life 22.2 / 12.9 / 8.7 / 7.6 / 7.4 / 7.3 h and
// intermediate (pi) half-life 0.67 / 0.62 / 0.61 / 0.59 / 0.55 / 0.53 h. Hence: (1) the pi
// half-life varies only between 0.53 and 0.67 h over three orders of magnitude of pssc, so it
// cannot be fitted (the target of Krogstad 1980, 0.43-1.48 h, is met at every pssc; non-
// identifiable) and V1, which is monotone in pssc, was chosen as the fitted observable; (2) at the
// V1 that fits (pssc 6.15e-4) the terminal half-life is about 20.5 h, so the predictions for the
// terminal half-life and the pi half-life below are NOT blind. The bisection result was seen. Not
// seen before writing the rest: every Healy and label concentration, the trough, the AUC rows
// that need the kernel, the GFR scaling rows and the budget.
//
// CRITERION as in the lithium test: |z| <= 2 on the inter-individual SD (SD taken from the
// "+/-" of the source), or a stated fold when there is no spread, or a stated range.
//
// PRE-RUN EXPECTATIONS
//  W1  terminal t1/2 (h)             ~20.5 (seen)     Healy 7.7 +/- 1.8: FAIL, z about +7
//  W2  terminal t1/2 vs label 4-6 h and Krogstad 4.7-11.2 h: FAIL (outside both ranges)
//  W3  pi half-life (h)              ~0.68 (seen)     Krogstad 0.43-1.48: pass (inside, not informative)
//  W4  total clearance (mL/min)      100.3 (arithmetic)  Healy 86.1 +/- 8.9 /1.73 m2: pass, z +1.6;
//                                    Rodvold 98.4: pass, fold 1.02; label 70.6: fold 1.42 (fail at 1.3)
//  W5  AUC over the interval (1 g)   166.2 = 1000/CL (arithmetic)  Healy 227 +/- 28.3: FAIL, z -2.2
//  W6  Healy concentration 1 h after the end of the infusion, 33.7 +/- 3.8: FAIL, predicted 45-75
//  W7  Healy trough 7.9 +/- 1.7: FAIL, predicted 15-40 (accumulation with t1/2 about 20 h)
//  W8  label 63 / 23 / 8 mg/L (end of infusion, 2 h after, 11 h after; fold 1.3): FAIL for all three
//  W9  CL vs CLcr (Matzke 1984, CL = 3.66 + 0.689 CLcr), cl_renal scaled by CLcr/117 (117 = the
//      creatinine clearance of the Golper subjects): CLcr 60: 56.9 vs 45.0 (fold 1.26, pass at 1.3);
//      CLcr 30: 34.1 vs 24.3 (fold 1.40, FAIL at 1.3). The kernel must reproduce dose/CL to 0.5 %.
//  W10 closed forms: AUC_inf = 1000/CL exactly (0.2 %), renal fraction of the AUC 0.887.
//  W11 pure interstitial space (kpsc = 1): about 11 L (the finding that V_ss 59 L exceeds the
//      interstitial space by a factor kpsc = 5.4: vancomycin is excluded from cells, so the excess
//      is unexplained by this pattern; it is not explained here).
//  W12 tissue penetration: Kp printed per organ; CSF:serum 0.18 (non-meningitis, Albanese 2000, from
//      the dossier, abstract not reopened, no SD) is printed, NOT asserted.
//  Structural statement written before the run: the failures W1, W5-W8 trace to one cause: the one
//  permeability scalar, fitted to a small V1, makes tissue equilibration slow, which lengthens the
//  terminal phase; a fast distribution (pssc 0.05, V1 about 50 L) reproduces t1/2 7.6 h but not V1.
//  The test prints that variant as a sensitivity, not asserting it as the model.
//
// OUTCOME AGAINST THE EXPECTATIONS (written after the first run; bands set from it, predictions
// above untouched). Terminal t1/2 20.3 h, pi 0.70 h, AUC 166.2, CL 100.3 and the GFR rows came out
// as written (W1, W2, W3, W4, W5, W9, W10, W11). WRONG IN DIRECTION: W6, W7, W8. The model gives
// LOWER concentrations than observed after the infusion, not higher: c(2 h) 21.0 vs 33.7 (z -3.3),
// trough 2.9 vs 7.9 (z -2.9), 11 h after 2.9 vs 8, 2 h after 11.3 vs 23, and HIGHER at the end of
// the infusion, 95.2 vs 63 (fold 1.5). Cause (diagnosed from the printed sensitivity, not tuned):
// the slow terminal phase (20 h) carries a small fraction of the AUC, since the small V1 holds the
// dose briefly in the central space and the permeability-limited tissue returns it slowly; the
// plasma between 2 h and 12 h is therefore set by the rapid phases, and falls too fast. The fast-
// distribution variant (pssc 0.05, V1 about 50 L) gives trough 7.1 (matches 7.9) and t1/2 7.6 h, but
// c(2 h) 18.7 (z -4): one scalar cannot give V1 10.95 L, t1/2 about 8 h and the Healy shape.
// W5: Healy's own numbers disagree: 1000 mg / 227 mg h/L = 4.40 L/h = 73 mL/min, not the 86.1 mL/min
// per 1.73 m2 it reports; the model clearance 100 mL/min is 1.16 SD above the second and 1.37 times
// the first. W4c: the label's 0.058 L/kg/h is 71 mL/min at 73 kg. W9b: the model intercept (renal
// 89/117 slope plus 11.3 non-renal) is above Matzke's 3.66 mL/min intercept; Matzke's cohort is
// patients and CLcr there is 24-h measured, not the 117 of the Golper subjects.
//
// Marker CIRC28_DRUG_VANCOMYCIN_PASS.

// ===================================================================================================
// ROUND 2. The ps scalar is now FITTED TO A RATE OBSERVABLE: the pooled terminal half-life of normal-
// renal-function studies, 7.69 h, u 0.64 h (Healy 1987 7.7; Krogstad 1980 midpoint 7.95; Matzke 1984 group I
// 9.1; Rotschafer 1982 6.0; computed in va_t12_pool; u = max(Healy SE 0.54, between-study SD 1.28/sqrt 4)).
// pssc = 0.03394 (offline bisection, stored). Kp scalar still fitted to V_ss 59.13 L; cl_renal observed;
// remainder declared. V1 (10.95 L Matzke 1986; 9.0 +/- 4.0 L Rotschafer 1982) and alpha (0.5 +/- 0.3 h
// Rotschafer 1982) are VALIDATION rows now. The Healy and Krogstad terminal half-lives are inside the
// pooled fit, so they are no longer validation rows.
// DISCLOSURE: before round 2 I had seen the round-1 scan (terminal t1/2 7.56 h and V1 50.6 L at pssc 0.05,
// t1/2 8.66 h and V1 33.1 L at 0.01) and the round-1 results below, so the round-2 predictions for pssc,
// V1 and trough are interpolations of seen numbers, not blind. The bisection printed only pssc (0.03394).
// Not seen: everything in the split diagnostic, the round-2 budget, c(2 h) and the label rows at the new pssc.
//
// COORDINATOR'S PREDICTION (recorded as theirs): with ps fitted to the terminal half-life the trough, AUC and
// post-infusion concentration rows pass or move inside fold 1.25; the CLcr 30 row improves but may still
// fail; the model's apparent central volume is larger than the 2-compartment V1 (10.95 L).
// MY PREDICTIONS (round 2, written before the round-2 run):
//  R1  peeled central volume V1 (bolus) 40-52 L: FAIL vs 10.95 (fold >= 3.5) and vs Rotschafer 9.0 +/- 4.0
//      (z > 7). Agrees with the coordinator's direction; the size is mine.
//  R2  alpha (intermediate) half-life 0.55-0.62 h: PASS vs Rotschafer 0.5 +/- 0.3 (|z| < 0.5), but not
//      informative (insensitive to pssc, round 1).
//  R3  Healy trough 6.5-8.0 (observed 7.9 +/- 1.7): PASS. Coordinator's prediction agreed.
//  R4  Healy c at 1 h after the end of the infusion 16-20 (observed 33.7 +/- 3.8): FAIL (z < -3.5). The
//      coordinator's prediction (inside fold 1.25) is DISAGREED: with V1 near 45 L the plasma at 1 h after
//      the infusion is about Dose/V_ss-like, about 18.
//  R5  AUC over the interval 166.2 = 1000/CL regardless of distribution: FAIL (z -2.15, fold 1.37). The
//      coordinator's prediction is DISAGREED: AUC does not depend on ps at all.
//  R6  label 63 / 23 / 8 mg/L: end of infusion 38-52 (FAIL, fold >= 1.2; at 52 pass at 1.25), 2 h after 14-18
//      (FAIL), 11 h after (= trough) 6.5-8.0 (PASS).
//  R7  CL vs CLcr rows: CL depends only on cl_renal x CLcr/117 + non-renal, not on ps: CLcr 60 fold 1.27
//      (pass at 1.3), CLcr 30 fold 1.40 (FAIL) UNCHANGED from round 1. Coordinator's "improves" DISAGREED.
//  R8  Budget: trough relative u falls from 75 % to 25-40 %; shares: CL renal 35-55 %, CL non-renal 20-35 %,
//      t1/2 observation 10-25 %, others < 5 %. AUC unchanged (14.3 %).
//  R9  Split diagnostic (labelled, not adopted unless each class has its own observable): fenestrated organs
//      (liver, kidney, lung, gut, spleen, pancreas) at a fast ps (pf = 0.5, NOT fitted) and the continuous
//      class (brain, heart, muscle, adipose, skin, bone, rest) fitted to the same pooled t1/2: the fenestrated
//      organs hold about 8 % of V_ss by the interstitial pattern (about 4.6 L), so V1 comes out about 9-13 L
//      (PASS vs 10.95 and 9.0 +/- 4.0), alpha 0.4-0.7 h, trough 6.5-9, Healy c(1 h after) 27-40 (PASS
//      vs 33.7 +/- 3.8), end of infusion 75-100 (FAIL vs label 63). If so, one scalar on the generic ps vector
//      cannot give alpha-beta together but two classes can; to ADOPT it the class scalar pf needs its own
//      observable; the only candidates are V1 (a volume) and alpha (non-identifiable): so NOT adopted.
// ===================================================================================================
// (The text ABOVE this block is round 1, superseded: pssc fitted to V1 = 10.95 L.)
// ROUND 2 OUTCOME (written after the round-2 run; bands set from it, predictions above untouched).
// pssc = 0.03394, terminal t1/2 7.6875 (fit). Hits: R1 V1 48.4 L (40-52), R2 alpha 0.61 h (0.55-0.62),
// R3 trough 7.08 (6.5-8.0), R4 c(1 h after) 18.5 (16-20, coordinator's inside-fold-1.25 prediction wrong),
// R5 AUC 166.2 fail, R6b 16.4 (14-18), R6c 7.08, R7 CL rows unchanged (56.92 / 34.10 vs 45.0 / 24.3, fold
// 1.26 / 1.40; coordinator's "improves" wrong: CL does not depend on ps), R8 trough relative u 30.5 %
// (25-40). Misses: R6a end of infusion 36.9 vs predicted 38-52 (observed label 63, fold 1.71, fail);
// R8 shares: CL renal 55.3 % (predicted 35-55), CL non-renal 38.0 % (20-35), t1/2 observation 1.7 %
// (predicted 10-25, wrong: the trough is nearly insensitive to the fitted half-life once the
// distribution is fast; the reason was not investigated further), V_ss 5.0 %; R9 split: V1 48.6 L (predicted 9-13, WRONG). Cause of the
// R9 miss: the fenestrated organs do hold only about 8 % of V_ss, but the 7.69 h half-life forces the
// continuous class to pc = 0.0339, which is also fast, so the early volume is still about 48 L. Making
// the continuous class slow enough for V1 10.95 L restores the 20 h terminal phase of round 1. The
// closed-form check (R10) shows why: with V1 10.95, V2 = 48.2 and CL 6.02 L/h, a 7.69 h half-life needs
// Q = 31.9 L/h; Q 5.7-9.3 L/h (patient models) give 10-12 h. The split is therefore not adopted.
// ===================================================================================================
// ROUND 3. Kernel unchanged; per organ the flow-limited state is now VASCULAR + INTERSTITIAL space
// (vf'_i = vas_i + int_i r / bp, r = 0.784 = fu + (1 - fu) x 0.28, Levitt 2003) and the permeability-
// limited state is a DEEP space with kp_i = kd int_i / (1 - vf'_i); kd fitted in closed form to V_ss
// 59.13 L, pssc refitted to the pooled terminal half-life 7.6875 h (offline bisection, stored:
// 0.0251534; the bisection printed only pssc). Derivation and sources: module header.
// EVERYTHING BELOW WAS WRITTEN BEFORE THE FIRST ROUND-3 RUN OF THIS TEST. Seen beforehand: rounds 1-2
// results, and the bisection output pssc = 0.0251534 (inside my predicted 0.025-0.045).
//
// COORDINATOR'S PREDICTIONS (recorded as theirs): apparent central volume falls to 12-22 L; end of the
// 60-min infusion of 1 g rises to 45-58 mg/L; 1 h after the infusion 26-36 mg/L; trough and terminal
// half-life stay passing; AUC stays 166 mg h/L and still fails against Healy's 227; the CLcr 30 row
// does not change.
// MY PREDICTIONS (reason: V_ss ln2 / CL = 6.81 h and the fitted 7.69 h is only 13 % above it, so the 48 L
// behind the barrier must still exchange nearly as fast as in round 2; only 8 L moved in front of it):
//  T1  fast space (bp x blood + r x interstitium) 10.5-11.5 L; kd 4.4-4.9
//  T2  peeled central volume V1 (bolus, 0.25-3 h residual) 40-50 L: FAIL vs 10.95 and 9.0 +/- 4.0.
//      Coordinator's 12-22 L DISAGREED.
//  T3  alpha half-life 0.50-0.65 h (pass vs Rotschafer 0.5 +/- 0.3, uninformative)
//  T4  end of infusion at steady state 35.5-39 mg/L: FAIL vs label 63 (fold about 1.7). Coordinator's 45-58
//      DISAGREED.
//  T5  1 h after the infusion 17.5-19.5: FAIL vs Healy 33.7 +/- 3.8 (z about -4). Coordinator's 26-36 DISAGREED.
//  T6  2 h after the infusion 15.5-17.5: FAIL vs label 23.
//  T7  trough 6.9-7.3: PASS (agreed). AUC interval 166.2: FAIL z -2.15 (agreed). CLcr 60 / 30: 56.9 / 34.1,
//      unchanged (agreed).
//  T8  pi phase: fine-grid bolus (1 mg over 0.01 h), second residual on 0.03-0.15 h (window fixed a priori):
//      half-life 0.06-0.11 h against the classical 7 min = 0.117 h (Matzke 1986 review, no SD): PASS at fold 2.
//  T9  budget: trough relative u 28-34 %; r and the interstitial scale together < 3 % of var(trough) and 0 %
//      of var(AUC); AUC relative u 14.3 % unchanged.
//  T10 identities asserted: mass balance of circ28_run below 1e-6 relative; V_ss = 59.13 L to 1e-9; fast
//      space + deep capacity = V_ss; CL = renal + remainder; AUC_inf = dose/CL to 0.2 %.
//  D1  ONE LABELLED DIAGNOSTIC, not the model, run only if T2/T4/T5 come out as I predict (i.e. the
//      coordinator's diagnosis fails). Candidate: the structure is not the problem; the INPUT PAIR (V_ss 59 L
//      from Matzke's patients, CL 100 mL/min from Golper + remainder) is not that of the subjects whose
//      concentrations are compared. Inputs replaced by the healthy-volunteer/label ones: total CL = dose / AUC
//      of Healy = 1000/227 = 4.405 L/h (both routes scaled, renal fraction kept), V_ss = label "distribution
//      coefficient" midpoint 0.365 L/kg x 73 = 26.6 L (whether that coefficient is a V_ss is not stated in
//      the label), kd closed form, pssc refitted to the same pooled 7.69 h (offline, stored). It uses two
//      validation observables as inputs, so it can NOT be adopted; it discriminates "structure" from
//      "inputs". Predicted from a two-compartment estimate (V1 11 L, V2 15.6 L, Q 2.4 L/h):
//      V1 9-14 L (PASS vs 10.95 at fold 1.5 and vs 9.0 +/- 4.0), alpha half-life 0.7-1.3 h, end of infusion
//      62-78 (PASS vs 63 at fold 1.25), 1 h after 36-46 (z +0.6 to +3.2 vs 33.7 +/- 3.8), 2 h after 23-30
//      (PASS vs 23 at 1.25 up to 28.7), trough 4.5-6.5 (z -2.0 to -0.8 vs 7.9 +/- 1.7; fold 0.56-0.81 vs label
//      8), AUC interval 227 by construction. If these hold, the round 1-3 shape failures are an input
//      inconsistency between populations, not a missing compartment.
//  NOT RE-RUN in round 3: the round-2 two-class split (R9) and the round-1 pssc sensitivity; their numbers
//  stay in the header above and in the report.
// ===================================================================================================
// ROUND 3 OUTCOME (written after the first round-3 run; bands set from it, predictions above untouched;
// the bands typed into t_sec_val before the run were my guesses and were replaced by measured ones).
// MINE, all inside the predicted ranges: fast space 11.01 L, kd 4.663, pssc 0.02515; V1 (bolus peel) 44.4 L
// (fold 4.06 vs 10.95, z +8.9 vs 9.0 +/- 4.0: FAIL); alpha 0.577 h; end of infusion 36.7 (fold 0.58 vs 63:
// FAIL); 1 h after 18.6 (z -3.97: FAIL); 2 h after 16.4 (fold 0.71: FAIL); trough 7.07 (z -0.49: PASS);
// AUC 166.2 (z -2.15: FAIL); CLcr 60 / 30 56.92 / 34.10 unchanged; pi half-life 0.0747 h = 4.5 min vs 7 min
// (fold 0.64: PASS at fold 2); trough relative u 30.8 %, r and interstitial scale 0.00001 % of var(trough).
// COORDINATOR: WRONG on the central volume (44.4 L, not 12-22), on the end of infusion (36.7, not 45-58) and
// on 1 h after (18.6, not 26-36); RIGHT on trough, half-life, AUC and the CLcr 30 row.
// Why the diagnosis fails, in numbers: round 2 -> round 3 moved 8.1 L in front of the barrier and the
// profile after 0.25 h is the same to 1 % (end of infusion 36.9 -> 36.7, 1 h after 18.5 -> 18.6, trough
// 7.08 -> 7.07). V_ss ln2/CL = 6.81 h against the fitted 7.69 h leaves no room for a slow deep space
// whatever sits in front of it. The fine-grid peel does find a minutes phase (4.5 min) and its initial
// volume 1/(P + A + B) is 10.4 L (lean_single: 4.3 min, 9.5 L, an unresolved engine divergence noted in the
// module at va_pi_of; the budget shares also differ by up to 0.3 points there), so read as THREE exponentials the model's initial volume is 10.4 L and
// the "48 -> 44 L" is what a TWO-exponential reading of 0.25-3 h returns; printed, not asserted, because
// the literature V1 values (Matzke 1986 review, Rotschafer 1982) come from two-compartment fits.
// D1 (diagnostic, not the model), all inside my predicted ranges: V1 13.3 L (PASS both), alpha 1.18 h
// (z +2.27 vs 0.5 +/- 0.3: FAIL), end of infusion 71.7 (fold 1.14: PASS), 1 h after 39.3 (z +1.47: PASS),
// 2 h after 26.5 (fold 1.15: PASS), trough 5.26 (z -1.55 vs Healy: PASS; fold 0.66 vs label 8: FAIL), AUC
// 227 (input). So with the healthy-volunteer/label CL and V_ss the SAME structure gives a small V1 and the
// observed early concentrations: the round 1-3 shape failures come from the input pair (V_ss 59 L of
// Matzke's patients with CL 100 mL/min), not from a missing compartment. NOT adopted: it takes Healy's AUC
// as an input and the label coefficient is not shown to be a V_ss.
use darwin_pbpk::circ28::*
use darwin_pbpk::circ28_kp::*
use darwin_pbpk::circ28_drug::*
use darwin_pbpk::circ28_drug_lithium::*
use darwin_pbpk::circ28_drug_vancomycin::*
use math::pure::{exp, ln}

fn t_abs(x: f64) -> f64 {
    if x < 0.0 { return 0.0 - x }
    return x
}

fn t_rel(tag: string, got: f64, want: f64, tol: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    let r = t_abs(got - want) / t_abs(want)
    print("  "); print(tag); print(": got "); print(got); print(" want "); print(want)
    print("  rel = "); println(r)
    if !(r <= tol) {
        println("  [FAIL]")
        return 1
    }
    return 0
}

// expect: 1 pass, 0 fail, 2 not asserted (printed only). sd > 0: |z| <= 2; else fold.
fn t_row(tag: string, pred: f64, obs: f64, sd: f64, fold: f64, expect: i32, band_lo: f64, band_hi: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var stat = pred / obs
    var pass = false
    if sd > 0.0 {
        stat = (pred - obs) / sd
        pass = t_abs(stat) <= 2.0
    } else {
        pass = stat <= fold && stat >= 1.0 / fold
    }
    print("  "); print(tag); print(": predicted "); print(pred); print("  observed "); print(obs)
    print("  ratio "); print(pred / obs)
    if sd > 0.0 {
        print("  z "); print(stat)
    }
    if pass { print("  PASS") } else { print("  FAIL") }
    var bad = 0
    if expect != 2 {
        if stat < band_lo || stat > band_hi {
            print("  [outside the asserted band]")
            bad = 1
        }
        if expect == 1 && !pass {
            print("  [expected pass]")
            bad = 1
        }
        if expect == 0 && pass {
            print("  [expected fail]")
            bad = 1
        }
    }
    println("")
    return bad
}

// range row: pass when lo <= pred <= hi; expect 1 pass, 0 fail; band on pred
fn t_range(tag: string, pred: f64, lo: f64, hi: f64, expect: i32, band_lo: f64, band_hi: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var bad = 0
    var pass = false
    if pred >= lo && pred <= hi { pass = true }
    print("  "); print(tag); print(": predicted "); print(pred); print("  observed range "); print(lo); print(" to "); print(hi)
    if pass { print("  PASS") } else { print("  FAIL") }
    if expect != 2 {
        if pred < band_lo || pred > band_hi {
            print("  [outside the asserted band]")
            bad = 1
        }
        if expect == 1 && !pass {
            print("  [expected pass]")
            bad = 1
        }
        if expect == 0 && pass {
            print("  [expected fail]")
            bad = 1
        }
    }
    println("")
    return bad
}

fn t_rname(i: i32) -> string {
    if i == 0 { return "MW" }
    if i == 5 { return "fu" }
    if i == 6 { return "B:P" }
    if i == 10 { return "cl renal" }
    if i == 11 { return "cl plasma (unidentified)" }
    if i == 12 { return "Kp scalar" }
    if i == 13 { return "ps scalar" }
    return "unused"
}


fn t_fill(d: &Circ28Drug, th: &![f64; 18]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < 18 {
        (*th)[i] = circ28_drug_value(d, i)
        i = i + 1
    }
    return 0
}

fn t_trapz(cs: &[f64; 1300], t_end: f64) -> f64 with Mut, Div {
    var a = 0.0
    var k: i32 = 1
    let ke = li_idx(t_end)
    while k <= ke {
        a = a + 0.5 * ((*cs)[k] + (*cs)[k - 1]) * (li_tgrid(k) - li_tgrid(k - 1))
        k = k + 1
    }
    return a
}

// 1000 mg over 1 h. rf scales cl_renal; psv > 0 overrides pssc (sensitivity); kp1 = 1 uses kpsc 1.
// m: 0 AUC_inf, 1 terminal t1/2, 2 pi half-life, 3 peeled V1 (this profile, 1 h infusion not a
// bolus: reported as the residual-fit intercept volume, informational), 4 V_area, 5 c(1 h), 6 c(2 h),
// 7 c(3 h), 8 c(12 h), 9 trapezoid AUC(0-312), 10 kernel AUC(0-312), 11 Cmax
fn t_single_cs(d: &Circ28Drug, rf: f64, psv: f64, kp1: i32, pf: f64, m: &![f64; 12], cs: &![f64; 1300]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var th: [f64; 18] = [0.0; 18]
    t_fill(d, &!th)
    th[CD_CLREN] = th[CD_CLREN] * rf
    if psv > 0.0 { th[CD_PSSC] = psv }
    if kp1 == 1 { th[CD_KPSC] = 1.0 }
    var p = va_params(&th)
    if pf > 0.0 { p = va_params_split(&th, pf) }
    var tail: [f64; 2] = [0.0; 2]
    let a = va_profile(p, 1000.0, 1.0, cs, &!tail)
    var pe: [f64; 4] = [0.0; 4]
    li_peel(cs, va_w_tlo(), va_w_thi(), va_w_alo(), va_w_ahi(), &!pe)
    var cm = 0.0
    var k: i32 = 1
    while k <= 120 {
        if (*cs)[k] > cm { cm = (*cs)[k] }
        k = k + 1
    }
    (*m)[0] = a + (*cs)[1296] / pe[0]
    (*m)[1] = 0.6931471805599453 / pe[0]
    (*m)[2] = 0.6931471805599453 / pe[2]
    (*m)[3] = 1000.0 / (pe[1] + pe[3])
    (*m)[4] = 1000.0 / (pe[0] * (pe[3] / pe[2] + pe[1] / pe[0]))
    (*m)[5] = (*cs)[li_idx(1.0)]
    (*m)[6] = (*cs)[li_idx(2.0)]
    (*m)[7] = (*cs)[li_idx(3.0)]
    (*m)[8] = (*cs)[li_idx(12.0)]
    (*m)[9] = t_trapz(cs, 312.0)
    (*m)[10] = a
    (*m)[11] = cm
    return 0
}

fn t_single(d: &Circ28Drug, rf: f64, psv: f64, kp1: i32, pf: f64, m: &![f64; 12]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var cs: [f64; 1300] = [0.0; 1300]
    return t_single_cs(d, rf, psv, kp1, pf, m, &!cs)
}

// steady state of 1000 mg over 1 h q12h. m: 0 trough, 1 c(1 h), 2 c(2 h), 3 c(3 h), 4 Cmax,
// 5 mean over the interval x 12 (trapezoid AUC over the interval)
fn t_ss(d: &Circ28Drug, rf: f64, psv: f64, pf: f64, m: &![f64; 6]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var cs: [f64; 1300] = [0.0; 1300]
    var mm: [f64; 12] = [0.0; 12]
    t_single_cs(d, rf, psv, 0, pf, &!mm, &!cs)
    var ss: [f64; 5] = [0.0; 5]
    li_ss_from(&cs, 1.0, 12.0, &!ss)
    (*m)[0] = ss[0]
    (*m)[1] = li_ss_c(&cs, 1.0, 12.0)
    (*m)[2] = li_ss_c(&cs, 2.0, 12.0)
    (*m)[3] = li_ss_c(&cs, 3.0, 12.0)
    (*m)[4] = ss[1]
    (*m)[5] = ss[4] * 12.0
    return 0
}

fn t_sec_record(d: &Circ28Drug) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    println("S0 parameter record (value, standard uncertainty, status)")
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < 18 {
        if i == 0 || i == 5 || i == 6 || i == 10 || i == 11 || i == 12 || i == 13 {
            print("  "); print(i); print(" "); print(t_rname(i)); print("  value "); print(circ28_drug_value(d, i))
            print("  u "); print(cd_sqrt(circ28_drug_variance(d, i))); print("  status "); println((*d).status[i])
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    return 0
}


fn t_sec_closed(d: &Circ28Drug, m: &![f64; 12]) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    let cl = (circ28_drug_value(d, CD_CLREN) + circ28_drug_value(d, CD_CLPLA))
    println("S2 closed forms: plasma CL = cl_renal + cl_unidentified")
    print("  total clearance (L/h) "); println(cl)
    fails = fails + t_rel("AUC_inf = Dose / CL", (*m)[0], 1000.0 / cl, 2.0e-3)
    fails = fails + t_rel("kernel AUC(0-312) vs trapezoid AUC(0-312)", (*m)[10], (*m)[9], 2.0e-3)
    print("  renal share of the AUC (CL_ren x AUC / dose): "); println(circ28_drug_value(d, CD_CLREN) * (*m)[0] / 1000.0)
    return fails
}

fn t_balance(d: &Circ28Drug) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var th: [f64; 18] = [0.0; 18]
    t_fill(d, &!th)
    let p = va_params(&th)
    var dc = circ28_dose_iv(1000.0, 1.0, 0.05, 3.0, 0.5, 120.0, 24.0, 96.0)
    let r = circ28_run(p, dc)
    return r.balance_err
}


// Closed-form two-compartment check (arithmetic only): V1 = 10.95 L, V2 = V_ss - V1, CL = total plasma
// clearance. beta half-life for several intercompartmental clearances Q (L/h), and the Q that gives the
// pooled terminal half-life.
fn t_beta12(cl: f64, v1: f64, v2: f64, q: f64) -> f64 with Mut, Div {
    let k10 = cl / v1
    let k12 = q / v1
    let k21 = q / v2
    let sm = k10 + k12 + k21
    let disc = sm * sm - 4.0 * k10 * k21
    let beta = 0.5 * (sm - cd_sqrt(disc))
    return 0.6931471805599453 / beta
}
fn t_sec_twocomp(d: &Circ28Drug) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    let cl = circ28_drug_value(d, CD_CLREN) + circ28_drug_value(d, CD_CLPLA)
    let v1 = va_obs_v1()
    let v2 = va_obs_vss() - v1
    println("R10 two-compartment closed form, V1 10.95 L, V2 = Vss - V1, CL = total plasma clearance")
    print("  limit Q -> infinity (one compartment of V_ss): t1/2 "); println(0.6931471805599453 * va_obs_vss() / cl)
    print("  Q 5.7 L/h (Mangin ICU): "); print(t_beta12(cl, v1, v2, 5.71)); print(" h;  Q 9.3 (Escobar): "); print(t_beta12(cl, v1, v2, 9.3)); print(" h;  Q 20: "); print(t_beta12(cl, v1, v2, 20.0)); print(" h;  Q 35: "); println(t_beta12(cl, v1, v2, 35.0))
    var lo = 1.0
    var hi = 1000.0
    var it: i32 = 0
    while it < 60 {
        let mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)
        if t_beta12(cl, v1, v2, mid) > va_obs_t12() { lo = mid } else { hi = mid }
        it = it + 1
    }
    let qn = 0.5 * (lo + hi)
    print("  Q needed for t1/2 = pooled 7.69 h with V1 10.95 L: "); print(qn); println(" L/h (literature Q 5.7-10 L/h are all patient populations)")
    if !(qn > 20.0 && qn < 60.0) {
        println("  [FAIL] Q band")
        fails = fails + 1
    }
    return fails
}


// W9: CL vs CLcr, cl_renal scaled by CLcr / 117
fn t_sec_gfr(d: &Circ28Drug) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    println("W9 clearance vs creatinine clearance (Matzke 1984: CL = 3.66 + 0.689 CLcr; cl_renal x CLcr/117)")
    var m1: [f64; 12] = [0.0; 12]
    var m2: [f64; 12] = [0.0; 12]
    t_single(d, 60.0 / 117.0, 0.0, 0, 0.0, &!m1)
    t_single(d, 30.0 / 117.0, 0.0, 0, 0.0, &!m2)
    let cl1 = 1000.0 / m1[0] / 0.06
    let cl2 = 1000.0 / m2[0] / 0.06
    print("  kernel CL at CLcr 60: "); print(cl1); print(" mL/min, t1/2 "); println(m1[1])
    print("  kernel CL at CLcr 30: "); print(cl2); print(" mL/min, t1/2 "); println(m2[1])
    fails = fails + t_rel("kernel CL = renal x f + non-renal, CLcr 60", cl1, va_cl_ren_mlmin() * 60.0 / 117.0 + va_cl_nr_mlmin(), 5.0e-3)
    fails = fails + t_rel("kernel CL = renal x f + non-renal, CLcr 30", cl2, va_cl_ren_mlmin() * 30.0 / 117.0 + va_cl_nr_mlmin(), 5.0e-3)
    fails = fails + t_row("W9a CL at CLcr 60 vs Matzke 3.66 + 0.689 x 60", cl1, 3.66 + 0.689 * 60.0, 0.0, 1.3, 1, 1.2, 1.32)
    fails = fails + t_row("W9b CL at CLcr 30 vs Matzke 3.66 + 0.689 x 30", cl2, 3.66 + 0.689 * 30.0, 0.0, 1.3, 0, 1.35, 1.45)
    return fails
}


fn t_slopes(d: &Circ28Drug, s: &![f64; 2]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let x = circ28_drug_value(d, CD_PSSC)
    let h = 1.0e-2 * x
    (*s)[0] = (va_t12_at(d, x + h) - va_t12_at(d, x - h)) / (2.0 * h)
    return 0
}

fn t_budget(d: &Circ28Drug, b: &![f64; 40]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var sl: [f64; 2] = [0.0; 2]
    t_slopes(d, &!sl)
    var th: [f64; 18] = [0.0; 18]
    t_fill(d, &!th)
    va_budget(&th, sl[0], b)
    return 0
}



fn t_zname(i: i32) -> string {
    if i == 0 { return "bp" }
    if i == 1 { return "CL renal (mL/min)" }
    if i == 2 { return "CL non-renal (mL/min)" }
    if i == 3 { return "Vss obs (L)" }
    if i == 4 { return "t1/2 obs (h)" }
    if i == 5 { return "r interstitial:plasma" }
    return "interstitial volume scale"
}

fn t_sec_fit(d: &Circ28Drug) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    var th: [f64; 18] = [0.0; 18]
    t_fill(d, &!th)
    let pl = va_params(&th)
    let bp = circ28_drug_value(d, CD_BP)
    let kd = circ28_drug_value(d, CD_KPSC)
    println("S1 molar arithmetic, the round-3 spaces and the fits")
    print("  1000 mg = "); print(1000.0 / va_mw()); print(" mmol at MW "); println(va_mw())
    print("  renal fraction of the plasma clearance used: "); println(va_cl_ren_mlmin() / (va_cl_ren_mlmin() + va_cl_nr_mlmin()))
    print("  non-renal estimates (mL/min): Rodvold 10.4, label "); print(va_nr_label()); print(", Golper 42; used "); print(va_cl_nr_mlmin())
    print(" u "); println(va_u_cl_nr_mlmin())
    print("  total clearance used (mL/min): "); println(va_cl_ren_mlmin() + va_cl_nr_mlmin())
    print("  r = fu + (1 - fu) K = "); print(va_r_int()); print(" u "); print(va_u_r()); print("; interstitial volume of the pattern (L) "); print(va_int_volume())
    print("; Levitt 2003 extracellular 17.45 L less plasma water "); print(va_plasma_water()); print(" L -> scale u "); println(va_u_isc())
    let fast = va_fast_volume(bp, va_r_int(), 1.0)
    let deep = kd * va_int_volume()
    print("  T1 fast space, plasma-referred (bp x blood + r x interstitium) "); print(fast); print(" L; deep capacity kd x interstitium "); print(deep); print(" L; kd "); println(kd)
    if !(fast > 10.5 && fast < 11.5) {
        println("  [FAIL] fast space outside the predicted 10.5-11.5 L")
        fails = fails + 1
    }
    if !(kd > 4.4 && kd < 4.9) {
        println("  [FAIL] kd outside the predicted 4.4-4.9")
        fails = fails + 1
    }
    fails = fails + t_rel("T10 fast space + deep capacity = V_ss", fast + deep, va_obs_vss(), 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + t_rel("T10 V_ss of the kernel (circ28_vss_plasma) = 0.81 x 73", circ28_vss_plasma(pl), va_obs_vss(), 1.0e-9)
    var o: [f64; 4] = [0.0; 4]
    va_peeled(&th, &!o)
    fails = fails + t_rel("peeled terminal t1/2 (h) = pooled 7.6875 (the pssc fit)", o[2], va_obs_t12(), 1.0e-6)
    var po: [f64; 3] = [0.0; 3]
    va_t12_pool(&!po)
    print("  pooled terminal t1/2: mean "); print(po[0]); print(" h, between-study SD "); print(po[1]); print(" h, u "); print(po[2]); println(" h")
    print("  bolus peel (validation, not fitted): alpha t1/2 "); print(o[0]); print(" h, V1 "); print(o[1]); print(" L, V_area "); print(o[3]); println(" L")
    print("  pssc "); print(circ28_drug_value(d, CD_PSSC)); print(" (round 2: "); print(va_pssc_round2()); println(")")
    return fails
}

// T8 pi phase from a fine-grid bolus
fn t_sec_pi(d: &Circ28Drug) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    var th: [f64; 18] = [0.0; 18]
    t_fill(d, &!th)
    var pe: [f64; 4] = [0.0; 4]
    var o: [f64; 3] = [0.0; 3]
    va_pi_of(&th, &!pe, &!o)
    println("T8 pi phase (1 mg over 0.01 h, second residual on 0.03-0.15 h; coarse-bolus A, B, alpha, lambda)")
    print("  points used "); print(o[2]); print("  intercept P (1/L) "); print(o[1]); print("  A "); print(pe[3]); print("  B "); print(pe[1])
    print("  volume 1/(P + A + B) (L) "); println(1.0 / (o[1] + pe[3] + pe[1]))
    fails = fails + t_row("T8 pi half-life (h) vs classical 7 min (fold 2)", o[0], 7.0 / 60.0, 0.0, 2.0, 1, 0.55, 0.75)
    return fails
}

fn t_sec_val(d: &Circ28Drug, m: &![f64; 12], ss: &![f64; 6]) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    let cl = (circ28_drug_value(d, CD_CLREN) + circ28_drug_value(d, CD_CLPLA))
    var th: [f64; 18] = [0.0; 18]
    t_fill(d, &!th)
    var o: [f64; 4] = [0.0; 4]
    va_peeled(&th, &!o)
    println("V validation, predicted vs observed (steady state of 1 g over 1 h q12h), ROUND 3")
    println("  terminal t1/2: Healy 7.7 and Krogstad 4.7-11.2 are INSIDE the pooled fit (not validation); label 4-6 h is not")
    fails = fails + t_range("W2a terminal t1/2 vs label 4-6 h           ", (*m)[1], 4.0, 6.0, 0, 7.5, 7.9)
    fails = fails + t_row("T2a V1 (bolus peel) vs Matzke 1986 10.95   ", o[1], va_obs_v1(), 0.0, 1.5, 0, 3.9, 4.2)
    fails = fails + t_row("T2b V1 (bolus peel) vs Rotschafer 9.0 +/- 4", o[1], va_val_v1_rot(), va_val_v1_rot_sd(), 0.0, 0, 8.5, 9.2)
    fails = fails + t_row("T3  alpha t1/2 (h) vs Rotschafer 0.5 +/- 0.3", o[0], va_val_alpha(), va_val_alpha_sd(), 0.0, 1, 0.1, 0.45)
    fails = fails + t_range("W3  alpha vs Krogstad pi 0.43-1.48 h       ", o[0], 0.43, 1.48, 1, 0.53, 0.63)
    fails = fails + t_row("W4a total CL (mL/min) Healy 86.1 +/- 8.9 ", cl / 0.06, 86.1, 8.9, 0.0, 1, 1.2, 2.0)
    fails = fails + t_row("W4b total CL (mL/min) Rodvold 98.4       ", cl / 0.06, 98.4, 0.0, 1.15, 1, 1.0, 1.05)
    fails = fails + t_row("W4c total CL (mL/min) label 0.058 L/kg/h ", cl / 0.06, 0.058 * 73.0 * 1000.0 / 60.0, 0.0, 1.3, 0, 1.35, 1.5)
    fails = fails + t_row("W5 AUC over the interval (mg h/L) Healy  ", (*ss)[5], 227.0, 28.3, 0.0, 0, -2.4, -1.9)
    fails = fails + t_row("T5 c at 1 h after end of infusion Healy  ", (*ss)[2], 33.7, 3.8, 0.0, 0, -4.2, -3.8)
    fails = fails + t_row("T7 trough Healy                          ", (*ss)[0], 7.9, 1.7, 0.0, 1, -0.7, -0.4)
    fails = fails + t_row("T4 label end of infusion (63), fold 1.25 ", (*ss)[1], 63.0, 0.0, 1.25, 0, 0.56, 0.61)
    fails = fails + t_row("T6 label 2 h after infusion (23)         ", (*ss)[3], 23.0, 0.0, 1.25, 0, 0.69, 0.75)
    fails = fails + t_row("T7c label 11 h after infusion (8)        ", (*ss)[0], 8.0, 0.0, 1.25, 1, 0.85, 0.92)
    print("  other reading of Healy 1 h (end of the infusion): c(1 h) = "); print((*ss)[1]); println(" mg/L vs 33.7; not asserted")
    return fails
}

// D1 LABELLED DIAGNOSTIC (not the model): healthy-volunteer/label inputs CL = 1000/227 L/h, V_ss = 0.365 x 73 L
fn t_pd_diag() -> f64 { return 0.000873349481067 }
fn t_diag_prof(th: &[f64; 18], m: &![f64; 12], cs: &![f64; 1300]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    let p = va_params(th)
    var tail: [f64; 2] = [0.0; 2]
    let a = va_profile(p, 1000.0, 1.0, cs, &!tail)
    var pe: [f64; 4] = [0.0; 4]
    li_peel(cs, va_w_tlo(), va_w_thi(), va_w_alo(), va_w_ahi(), &!pe)
    (*m)[0] = a + (*cs)[1296] / pe[0]
    (*m)[1] = 0.6931471805599453 / pe[0]
    return 0
}
fn t_diag_ss(th: &[f64; 18], m: &![f64; 12], s6: &![f64; 6]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    var cs: [f64; 1300] = [0.0; 1300]
    t_diag_prof(th, m, &!cs)
    var ss: [f64; 5] = [0.0; 5]
    li_ss_from(&cs, 1.0, 12.0, &!ss)
    (*s6)[0] = ss[0]
    (*s6)[1] = li_ss_c(&cs, 1.0, 12.0)
    (*s6)[2] = li_ss_c(&cs, 2.0, 12.0)
    (*s6)[3] = li_ss_c(&cs, 3.0, 12.0)
    (*s6)[4] = ss[1]
    (*s6)[5] = ss[4] * 12.0
    return 0
}
fn t_sec_diag(d: &Circ28Drug) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    var th: [f64; 18] = [0.0; 18]
    t_fill(d, &!th)
    let cl0 = th[CD_CLREN] + th[CD_CLPLA]
    let cld = 1000.0 / 227.0
    let vssd = 0.365 * 73.0
    th[CD_CLREN] = th[CD_CLREN] * cld / cl0
    th[CD_CLPLA] = th[CD_CLPLA] * cld / cl0
    th[CD_KPSC] = va_kpsc_for(th[CD_BP], vssd)
    th[CD_PSSC] = t_pd_diag()
    var o: [f64; 4] = [0.0; 4]
    va_peeled(&th, &!o)
    var m: [f64; 12] = [0.0; 12]
    var ss: [f64; 6] = [0.0; 6]
    t_diag_ss(&th, &!m, &!ss)
    println("D1 LABELLED DIAGNOSTIC, NOT THE MODEL: inputs CL = 1000/227 L/h (Healy dose/AUC), V_ss = 0.365 L/kg x 73 (label midpoint), pssc refitted to 7.69 h")
    print("  CL "); print(cld); print(" L/h  V_ss "); print(vssd); print(" L  kd "); print(th[CD_KPSC]); print("  pssc "); print(th[CD_PSSC]); print("  V_ss ln2/CL "); print(0.6931471805599453 * vssd / cld); println(" h")
    print("  terminal t1/2 "); print(o[2]); print(" h  alpha t1/2 "); print(o[0]); print(" h  V1 "); print(o[1]); print(" L  AUC_inf "); println(m[0])
    fails = fails + t_rel("D1 terminal t1/2 = pooled 7.6875 (refit)", o[2], va_obs_t12(), 1.0e-5)
    fails = fails + t_row("D1a V1 vs Matzke 10.95 (fold 1.5)          ", o[1], va_obs_v1(), 0.0, 1.5, 1, 1.15, 1.28)
    fails = fails + t_row("D1b V1 vs Rotschafer 9.0 +/- 4             ", o[1], va_val_v1_rot(), va_val_v1_rot_sd(), 0.0, 1, 0.9, 1.25)
    fails = fails + t_row("D1c alpha vs Rotschafer 0.5 +/- 0.3        ", o[0], va_val_alpha(), va_val_alpha_sd(), 0.0, 0, 2.0, 2.5)
    fails = fails + t_row("D1d end of infusion vs label 63 (fold 1.25)", ss[1], 63.0, 0.0, 1.25, 1, 1.09, 1.19)
    fails = fails + t_row("D1e c 1 h after infusion vs Healy 33.7     ", ss[2], 33.7, 3.8, 0.0, 1, 1.2, 1.75)
    fails = fails + t_row("D1f 2 h after infusion vs label 23         ", ss[3], 23.0, 0.0, 1.25, 1, 1.10, 1.20)
    fails = fails + t_row("D1g trough vs Healy 7.9 +/- 1.7            ", ss[0], 7.9, 1.7, 0.0, 1, -1.8, -1.3)
    fails = fails + t_row("D1h trough vs label 8 (fold 1.25)          ", ss[0], 8.0, 0.0, 1.25, 0, 0.62, 0.70)
    fails = fails + t_row("D1i AUC interval vs Healy 227 (input)      ", ss[5], 227.0, 28.3, 0.0, 1, -0.1, 0.1)
    return fails
}

fn t_sec_tissue(d: &Circ28Drug) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var th: [f64; 18] = [0.0; 18]
    t_fill(d, &!th)
    let p = va_params(&th)
    println("W12 tissue penetration: long-time whole-organ:plasma ratio bp vf' + (1 - vf') kp (printed, not asserted)")
    print("  kidney "); print(p.bp * p.vf[2] + (1.0 - p.vf[2]) * p.kp[2]); print("  brain "); print(p.bp * p.vf[3] + (1.0 - p.vf[3]) * p.kp[3])
    print("  lung "); print(p.bp * p.vf[5] + (1.0 - p.vf[5]) * p.kp[5]); print("  muscle "); print(p.bp * p.vf[6] + (1.0 - p.vf[6]) * p.kp[6])
    print("  bone "); print(p.bp * p.vf[10] + (1.0 - p.vf[10]) * p.kp[10]); print("  skin "); println(p.bp * p.vf[9] + (1.0 - p.vf[9]) * p.kp[9])
    println("  observed, not asserted (no SD in the sources, abstracts only): CSF:serum 0.18 non-meningitis (Albanese 2000, dossier);")
    println("  sternal bone 9.3 +/- 3.0 ug/g (n = 10, no matched serum in the abstract)")
    return 0
}

fn t_sec_budget(b: &![f64; 40]) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    println("S6 uncertainty budget with refit (7 inputs; kd closed form, pssc by two chords on the terminal t1/2)")
    let ua = cd_sqrt((*b)[37])
    let ut = cd_sqrt((*b)[38])
    print("  AUC_inf (1000 mg) "); print((*b)[0]); print(" mg h/L  u "); print(ua); print("  (rel "); print(ua / (*b)[0]); println(")")
    print("  steady-state trough (1 g over 1 h q12h) "); print((*b)[1]); print(" mg/L  u "); print(ut); print("  (rel "); print(ut / (*b)[1]); println(")")
    println("  input                    u          share of var(AUC) %   share of var(trough) %")
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < 7 {
        print("  "); print(t_zname(i)); print("   "); print((*b)[30 + i]); print("   "); print(100.0 * (*b)[2 + i] / (*b)[37])
        print("   "); println(100.0 * (*b)[9 + i] / (*b)[38])
        i = i + 1
    }
    let rt = ut / (*b)[1]
    let sh = 100.0 * ((*b)[14] + (*b)[15]) / (*b)[38]
    if !(rt > 0.2 && rt < 0.45) {
        println("  [FAIL] trough relative u outside 0.20-0.45")
        fails = fails + 1
    }
    if !(sh < 10.0) {
        println("  [FAIL] r + interstitial scale share of var(trough) above 10 %")
        fails = fails + 1
    }
    return fails
}

fn main() -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    var d = circ28_drug_new()
    va_drug_into(&!d)
    var m1: [f64; 12] = [0.0; 12]
    t_single(&d, 1.0, 0.0, 0, 0.0, &!m1)
    fails = fails + t_sec_record(&d)
    fails = fails + t_sec_fit(&d)
    fails = fails + t_sec_closed(&d, &!m1)
    let be = t_balance(&d)
    print("  T10 mass balance of the IV run (circ28_run): "); println(be)
    if !(t_abs(be) < 1.0e-6) {
        println("  [FAIL] mass balance")
        fails = fails + 1
    }
    fails = fails + t_sec_pi(&d)
    var ss: [f64; 6] = [0.0; 6]
    t_ss(&d, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0, &!ss)
    fails = fails + t_sec_val(&d, &!m1, &!ss)
    fails = fails + t_sec_diag(&d)
    fails = fails + t_sec_twocomp(&d)
    fails = fails + t_sec_gfr(&d)
    fails = fails + t_sec_tissue(&d)
    var bud: [f64; 40] = [0.0; 40]
    t_budget(&d, &!bud)
    fails = fails + t_sec_budget(&!bud)
    if fails == 0 {
        println("CIRC28_DRUG_VANCOMYCIN_PASS")
        return 0
    }
    println("CIRC28_DRUG_VANCOMYCIN_FAIL")
    return 1
}
